    "Here are the search results for Vulkan compute machine learning with PyTorch, ncnn on Windows AMD GPU:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Kompute Framework\nMany ML & DL projects like PyTorch, TensorFlow, Alibaba DNN, and Tencent NCNN have either integrated or are looking to integrate the Vulkan SDK to add mobile and cross-vendor GPU support.(no content)Kompute is a general purpose GPU compute framework built on Vulkan to support 1000s of cross vendor graphics cards (AMD, Qualcomm, NVIDIA & friends).(no content)The project is backed by the Linux Foundation.\n\n### PyTorch Vulkan Support\nVulkan, being a cross-platform API, can work with a broader range of GPUs, including those from AMD, Intel, and ARM.(no content)PyTorch Vulkan provides a powerful way to accelerate machine learning models on a wide range of GPUs.\n\nThere's also a specific GitHub repository ([pytorch-win64-amd-vulkan](https://github.com/inzlukasz/pytorch-win64-amd-vulkan)) that provides tensors and dynamic neural networks in Python with strong GPU acceleration for AMD Vulkan on Windows 64-bit.\n\n### ncnn Vulkan\nVulkan is considered more portable and well supported by vendors as a cross-platform low-overhead graphics API. As a contrast, CUDA is only available on NVIDIA devices, Metal is only available on macOS and iOS, while loading OpenCL library is banned in Android 7.0+ and does not work on iOS.(no content)ncnn-vulkan supports Vulkan API GPU acceleration with 8-bit quantization and half-precision float storage, and can import models from caffe/pytorch/mxnet/onnx/darknet/keras/tensorflow(mlir). The package is available on PyPI with Windows 64-bit wheels available.\n\n### ExecuTorch Vulkan Backend\nThe ExecuTorch Vulkan delegate is a native GPU delegate for ExecuTorch built on top of the cross-platform Vulkan GPU API standard. It is primarily designed to leverage the GPU to accelerate model inference on Android devices, but can be used on any platform that supports Vulkan: laptops, servers, and edge devices.(no content)The aim of the Vulkan Compute Library is to provide GPU implementations for PyTorch operators via GLSL compute shaders.\n\n### Why Vulkan for ML?\nVarious mobile AI inference frameworks use Vulkan compute to drive the GPU, including Tencent ncnn, Alibaba MNN, and PyTorch Mobile. ncnn is exceptional here for its model/feature coverage and its production usage in Tencent apps.(no content)Using Vulkan for ML is possible today by using compute shaders to implement various algebra operations. Examples include Tencent/ncnn, Alibaba/MNN, and Unity ML."
